[{"label":"Error analysis at corpus scale","html":"<article class=\"paper\" aria-labelledby=\"pb-title\">\n  <header class=\"paper-hero\">\n    <p class=\"paper-venue\"\n      ><span class=\"badge\" data-variant=\"secondary\">Short paper</span\n      ><span>defuss-shadcn · <time datetime=\"2026-10\">October 2026</time></span></p\n    >\n    <h1 class=\"paper-title\" id=\"pb-title\"\n      >Error Analysis at Corpus Scale<span class=\"paper-title-sub\"\n        >Browsing every utterance of an evaluation in the paper itself</span\n      ></h1\n    >\n    <ul class=\"paper-authors\"\n      ><li>Aron Homberg</li\n      ><li>Claude</li></ul\n    >\n  </header>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-abstract\" aria-labelledby=\"pb-abstract\">\n    <h2 id=\"pb-abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n    <p\n      >A word error rate is an average; the errors are in the utterances. We show how a reader can browse all of them in\n      the paper: a grid of 100,000 utterances with their speaker, source, duration and errors, and a tree of the corpus\n      they come from. The data here is synthetic - generated deterministically - so that the page stays small and every\n      reader sees the same rows.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <nav class=\"paper-toc\" aria-labelledby=\"pb-toc\">\n    <h2 id=\"pb-toc\">Contents</h2>\n    <ol>\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pb-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>Every utterance</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pb-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>The corpus</a></li\n      >\n      <li\n        ><a href=\"#pb-cite\"><span class=\"paper-num\">·&nbsp;</span>Citation and references</a></li\n      >\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section typeset\" lang=\"en\" data-leading=\"tight\" data-align=\"justify\" aria-labelledby=\"pb-s1\">\n    <h2 id=\"pb-s1\"><span class=\"paper-num\">1&nbsp;</span>Every utterance</h2>\n    <div class=\"paper-wide\">\n      <div\n        class=\"data-grid\"\n        id=\"pb-grid\"\n        aria-label=\"Evaluation utterances\"\n        data-empty-text=\"No utterance matches.\"\n        style=\"height: 22rem\"\n      >\n        <div class=\"data-grid-viewport\">\n          <div class=\"data-grid-head\">\n            <div class=\"data-grid-row\">\n              <div\n                class=\"data-grid-header\"\n                data-field=\"id\"\n                data-type=\"number\"\n                data-format=\"\"\n                data-width=\"6rem\"\n                data-filter=\"number\"\n                data-locked\n                >Utterance</div\n              >\n              <div class=\"data-grid-header\" data-field=\"source\" data-width=\"10rem\" data-filter=\"select\">Source</div>\n              <div class=\"data-grid-header\" data-field=\"speaker\" data-width=\"8rem\" data-filter=\"text\">Speaker</div>\n              <div\n                class=\"data-grid-header\"\n                data-field=\"seconds\"\n                data-type=\"number\"\n                data-width=\"6rem\"\n                data-filter=\"number\"\n                >Seconds</div\n              >\n              <div class=\"data-grid-header\" data-field=\"words\" data-type=\"number\" data-width=\"6rem\" data-filter=\"number\"\n                >Words</div\n              >\n              <div\n                class=\"data-grid-header\"\n                data-field=\"errors\"\n                data-type=\"number\"\n                data-width=\"6rem\"\n                data-filter=\"number\"\n                >Errors</div\n              >\n              <div class=\"data-grid-header\" data-field=\"wer\" data-type=\"number\" data-width=\"6rem\" data-filter=\"number\"\n                >WER %</div\n              >\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"data-grid-body\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <p\n      >Sorting by WER puts the hardest utterances first; filtering a source and a minimum duration narrows the analysis\n      without leaving the page.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"paper-section typeset\" lang=\"en\" data-leading=\"tight\" data-align=\"justify\" aria-labelledby=\"pb-s2\">\n    <h2 id=\"pb-s2\"><span class=\"paper-num\">2&nbsp;</span>The corpus</h2>\n    <div\n      class=\"data-tree\"\n      id=\"pb-tree\"\n      aria-label=\"Corpus\"\n      data-empty-text=\"Nothing matches.\"\n      style=\"height: 16rem\"\n    ></div>\n    <p\n      >Three sources, a hundred speaker groups each, ten speakers per group and thirty utterances per speaker - 93,303\n      nodes - the hierarchy a reviewer walks to find where the errors cluster.</p\n    >\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"paper-bibtex\" aria-labelledby=\"pb-cite\">\n    <h2 id=\"pb-cite\">Citation and references</h2>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"bibtex apa mla ieee\" aria-label=\"Cite this paper\">\n      <figcaption>Cite this paper</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@techreport{homberg2026corpus,\n  title = {Error Analysis at Corpus Scale},\n  author = {Homberg, Aron and Claude},\n  institution = {defuss},\n  year = {2026},\n  month = oct,\n  url = {https://shadcn.defuss.org/papers/paper-big-data.html}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n    <figure class=\"bibtex\" data-formats=\"ieee apa bibtex\" data-format=\"ieee\" aria-label=\"References\">\n      <figcaption>References</figcaption>\n      <pre><code class=\"bibtex-source\">@inproceedings{ardila2020commonvoice,\n  author = {Ardila, Rosana and Branson, Megan and Davis, Kelly and Henretty, Michael and Kohler, Michael and Meyer, Josh and Morais, Reuben and Saunders, Lindsay and Tyers, Francis M. and Weber, Gregor},\n  title = {Common Voice: A Massively-Multilingual Speech Corpus},\n  booktitle = {Proceedings of the 12th Language Resources and Evaluation Conference},\n  pages = {4218--4222},\n  year = {2020}\n}\n\n@misc{homberg2026redeschrift,\n  author = {Homberg, Aron},\n  title = {Redeschrift 1.0: German speech recognition for every device},\n  year = {2026},\n  howpublished = {Hugging Face},\n  url = {https://huggingface.co/kyr0/redeschrift-1.0}\n}\n\n@misc{homberg2026defussshadcn,\n  author = {Homberg, Aron},\n  title = {defuss-shadcn: shadcn-style components as semantic HTML},\n  year = {2026},\n  howpublished = {GitHub},\n  url = {https://github.com/kyr0/defuss-shadcn}\n}</code></pre>\n    </figure>\n  </section>\n</article>\n","individual":false}]
